{"id":"8bfcc9b8c0968ecbfae72783b9cc5f21bc1d074ea6e7ae400c67a7c9b502924d","at":"2026-10-27T05:46:43Z","commit":"963a1431394075ffe9fcbe06375bacfbcc51619a","parents":["42ad614527e9caf2243acbc10ffbe8eba3c2f0200e93feb700a4ec023781ccf4"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Auth.Ash.BackendTest: sessions in the token resource: a token's row must be its own, with Macaw's metadata; its user is read as now","hash":"1dd4ae29"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-sessions.md#ash-sessions-fetch","hash":"556270f4"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"roles changed after sign-in are what fetch reports (the user as now); a row whose subject was rewritten by SQL is :invalid by token while fetch_by_id resolves the row's own subject; a row whose extra_data lost Macaw's metadata is :invalid both ways; a deleted user's sessions are :invalid both ways","basis":"review"}
{"id":"efa1a7c62deb3166c7c084c92dd436532e35ffb877b0c22b908bd279bee81a09","at":"2026-10-27T05:46:45Z","commit":"963a1431394075ffe9fcbe06375bacfbcc51619a","parents":["7605714c3fbb792695974697bf799ff45aecc11c06f2b329535201b03337f6ab"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Auth.Ash.BackendTest: sessions in the token resource: enrolling passes the second factor; other steps are kept once, read back only if known","hash":"5b5ad2e5"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-sessions.md#ash-sessions-steps","hash":"54d690f2"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":":second_factor_enroll sets second_factor_passed; :password_change twice is stored once; a step outside Macaw.Auth.steps/0 is stored (row's completed_steps) but never read back as an atom. The revoked-between-read-and-write race is not checked (no seam)","basis":"review"}
